course: dictionary
lesson: 3841
title: Forty: a number and a phrase
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Forty is a number word. It means 40, which is four tens. «Theo turned the router off and on forty times in one evening.» Here forty tells you how many times, so it is a quantity.
explain: You can make forty in different ways. 4 × 10 = 40 and 5 × 8 = 40 both give forty. Forty minutes, forty pages and forty times are all counts of things.
explain: Forty also appears in everyday phrases. «Sam's grandad and his brother Roy fell out for forty years.» Here forty years means a very long time. «Forty winks» means a short nap, so the number inside it is not being counted.
fact: Forty means 40, which is four tens.
fact: 40 = 4 × 10 = 5 × 8.
fact: «Forty winks» means a short nap.
fact: The «Roaring Forties» are strong winds between about 40 and 50 degrees south, which sailors used to race east.
fact: A number word can give a quantity, or it can be part of a phrase with a different meaning.
exercise: «Theo turned the router off and on forty times in one evening.» How many times did he do it? | *40 | 10 | 4 | 400
exercise: Which sum makes forty? | 4 + 10 | 50 − 8 | *5 × 8 | 5 + 8
exercise: «Zara read for forty minutes.» What does forty tell you here? | The name of a book | A short nap | *A count of minutes | A kind of game
test: «Sam's grandad and his brother Roy fell out for forty years.» How long did they fall out? | Forty winks | Four years | Forty minutes | *Forty years, a very long time
test: What does «forty winks» mean? | *A short nap | Four tens of games | Forty minutes of reading | Forty sleeps in a row
exam: Which statement about forty is true? | Forty is always the number 4 | *Forty is the number 40, four tens, and it can also be part of phrases like «forty winks» | Forty only ever means a short nap | Forty is the number 14
